      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-01-16_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <head>KIND STRANGER.</head>
        <p>THE KIND STRANGER.</p>
        <p>This is a beautiful story of a true incident which happened in Vienna, the capital of Austria. You know that Austria is now fight- ing against us, but she has not always had evil- minded rulers. , It was a cold winter's night. A tall man, wrapped in a cloak, was passing along the street when suddenly a poor ragged boy came flying past, and then., catching sight of the tall man, ran up to him and panted imploringly : "One guilder, good sir; just one, for pity's sake !". He hung back a little as he spoke, as if fear- ing that his petition might be answered with a hard word or even with a hard blow. But the</p>
