      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-01-16_WidnesExaminer_art0228" n="art0228">
        <head>HOMING PIGEON SOCIETIES. Meeting of West Lancashire Federation.</head>
        <p>HOMING PIGEON SOCIETIES. Meeting of West Lancashire Federation.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of the West Laneashire (Saturday) Federation of Homing Pigeon Socie- ties was held recently, The officials for 1915 were elected as follows :—President, Mr. William J. Shaw (Warrington); vice-presidents, Mr. H. J. Longton (Earlestown), Mr. ,James Lowe (Low- ton), Mr. Fred Boyle (Warrington), Mr. John Traverse (Burtonwood), Mr. William Wright (Latchford), Mr. Thomas Newton (Lymm), and Mr. Thomas Malkin (Warrington); vice-chair- pan, Mr. R. Taylor; convoyer, Mr. Sidney Tay- lor (11, Eastford-road, Lower Walton, near War- rington); assistant convoyer, iir. F. Bbyle; secretary, Mr. William IT. Paice (14, Miller- street, Warrington); treasukr, Mr. Thomas Malkin (Royal Exchange, Warrington); audit- ors, Messrs. George Crank and W. Stringfellow ; Lancashire Combination delegates, the President and the Secretary.</p>
        <p>The Federation Emergency Committee is corn- posed of the President, the Vice-presidents, the Vice-chairman, the Secretary, Mr. J. Williams (Bnrtonwood), Mr. Frank Jones (Frodsham), and Mr. R. Briggs (Frodsham). The matter of the race dates and stages was left to another meeting.</p>
      </div>
