        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. EDUCATION COMMITTEE. Tenders are invited for the ELECTRIC LIGHTING and ELECTRIC BELL installa- tions required at the OAKWOOD-AVENUE COUNCIL SCHOOL, Warrington (architects, Messrs. Wright and Hamlyn, Sankey-street, Warrington). Specifications and forms of, tender may be obtained on payment of a deposit of Half-a- guinea (which will be returned on deposit of a bona-fide tender) from the undersigned. Tenders must be forwarded on the forms and in the en- velope provided by not later than noon on Friday, the 29th January, 1915. Plans of the School can be seen and, if neces- sary, further particulars obtained from the Electrical Engineer (Mr. F. V. L. Mathias, Electricity Department. Warrington). . J. MOORE, MURRAY, • Secretary and Director. Education Office, Warrington, 15th January, 1915.</p>
        <p>R UNCORN UNION. -Kt MASTER'S ASSISTANT AND PORTER. The Guardians require a single man to under- take the duties of Master's Assistant and Porter at their Workhouse at Dutton, near Warring- ton. Salary, £3O per annum, with board, lodgings and washing, subject to the Poor Law Officers' Superannuation Act, 1896. • Further particulars may be obtained from the Master of the Workhouse (Mr. E. F. Parsons). Applications, stating age and previous occupa- tion, accompanied by not more than three recent testimonials, to be sent to, my Office, 71, tligh= street. Runcorn, not later than Monday, the 25th day of January, 1915. 2 By order, W. E. HOUGH, Acting Clerk to the Guardians. Union Offices, Runcorn, 14th January, 1915.</p>
        <p>CiOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. • TO STORES CONTRACTORS, EARTHENWARE PIPE MANUFACTURERS, QUARRY OWNERS, MERCHANTS, TEAM OWNERS, &amp;e. The Paving and Sewerage Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for the supply -of the Committee's requirements during the twelve months ending March 31st, 1916, viz.:— BLUE BRICKS. CHEQUERED TILES. • SEWER PIPES, BENDS, JUNCTIONS, &amp;c. MACADAM and CHIPPINGS. • ,LIMEIVONE CHTPPINGS. COPPER SLAG. PORTLAND CEMENT. CAST IRON GULLIES, &amp;c. BRUSHES, HAMMERS, SCUTCHES. &amp;c. SCAVENGERS' BROOMS, SHOVELS, SCUFFLES. and SCOOPS. &amp;c. STREET SWEEPING MACHINE ROTARY BROOMS. Also for CARTING for the Highway and Scavenging Departments for the twelve months. Parties wishing for tender forms will please specify THOSE MATERIALS ONLX for which they propose to tender. Specifications and samples may be seen and forms of tender and all further information ob- tained at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall. on and after Tuesday, the 19th inst., at which place tenders, sealed in the envelopes supplied, must be delivered on or before 12 o'clock noon on Monday, the Ist day of February, 1915. Any Contractor whose tender may be accepted will be required to observe the recognised cus- toms and conditions as to rate of wages and working hours prevailing within the Borough. The Committee reserve the right to divide the contracts in any way they may think fit, and do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. ANDREW M. KER, Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor. Borough Engineer &amp; Surveyor's Office, January 15th, 1915.</p>
        <p>IN the matter of a DEED OF ASSIGNMENT for the benefit of Creditors, executed on the 28th day of December, 1914, by GEORGE WALLINGTON of FROGHALL-LANE, WAR- RINGTON, Builder. The Creditors of the above-named GEORGE WALLINGTON who have not already sent in their claims, are required on or before the 28th 'day of January, 1915, to send in their names and ad- dresses, and the particulars of their debts or claims, to me, the undersigned, LOUIS ADRIAN VOISEY, of 5, Bold-street, Warrington. Chartered Account- ant, the Trustee under the said Deed, or in default thereof they will be excluded from the benefit of the dividend about to be declared. Dated this 14th day of January. 1915. LOUIS ADRIAN VOISEY, Trustee.</p>
